<Layout title="Equipment-hire guide"><article class="guide"><p class="eyebrow">FIELD NOTES / 01</p><h1>Plan the kit around<br/>the production.</h1><p class="lead">A camera is only part of a useful equipment list. Think through the room, the sound and the time your crew will have.</p><section><h2>Start with the shot</h2><p>For an interview, pair the cinema camera with the portrait lens and a video tripod. A locked frame gives your crew time to focus on the conversation.</p></section><section><h2>Control the light and sound</h2><p>An LED panel and light stand create a repeatable setup. Add a shotgun microphone and audio recorder when the location sound matters. Each light stand should carry its supplied sandbag.</p></section><section><h2>Count complete hire days</h2><p>The example charges each item's daily rate for every selected hire day. Save a quote to capture the catalogue rates at that revision. Saving again reprices the full quote at current rates.</p></section><div class="alert">This synthetic catalogue creates draft quotes. It does not reserve equipment or take payment.</div><a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Build your equipment quote</a></article></Layout>
